# Force LF in the working tree for Markdown files regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# `oclif readme` regenerates the command block between the <!-- commands -->
# and <!-- commandsstop --> tags using the regex `<!-- commands -->(.|\n)*<!--
# commandsstop -->`. In JS regex, `.` excludes ALL line terminators including
# `\r`, so `(.|\n)*` cannot cross a CRLF line ending. On a CRLF README the
# collapse match fails, the old block is never removed, and oclif prepends a
# fresh block above the stale one -> duplicated commands every run. Keeping
# Markdown as LF in the working tree avoids this.
*.md text eol=lf
